WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.334
I don't have to tell you --

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:04.133
I don't have to tell
anybody here. It's hot outside.

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:05.234
We're in the dog days of summer.

00:00:05.234 --> 00:00:06.868
It's hot, it's muggy,
it's gross.

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:09.901
Everyone's dragging.
And that includes my writers.

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:12.634
You know, they write hundreds
of jokes everyday just to get

00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:14.534
the 10 or 12 we end up
using in the monologue.

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:17.868
And honestly, a lot of the
jokes, we have to discard.

00:00:17.868 --> 00:00:19.267
They just aren't good.

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:21.400
And sometimes I think
they wrote them just to

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.267
throw in a few stinkers
to meet the page assignment.

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:27.267
And just because the air
outside feels like dog breath,

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:29.033
that doesn't mean
we can tolerate laziness,

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:32.067
which means it's time for
another "Surprise Inspection."

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:33.767
[ Bugle plays ]

00:00:37.734 --> 00:00:39.734
So here's how this works.

00:00:39.734 --> 00:00:41.701
I'm going to read
some real jokes

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:45.133
that were really submitted
by my real writers

00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:46.868
that are unusable for the show.

00:00:46.868 --> 00:00:50.567
Some are dumb, some are
offensive, some are confusing.

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:53.300
Most importantly, the writers
don't know we're doing this.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.133
And because most of them
don't watch the show,

00:00:56.133 --> 00:00:57.601
they'll never know.

00:00:57.601 --> 00:01:00.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:02.334
So let's get started.

00:01:02.334 --> 00:01:05.901
A fan has been banned from
the Colorado Avalanche's arena

00:01:05.901 --> 00:01:08.701
in Denver after
he allegedly spread the ashes

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:11.534
of his best friend on the ice
at a game.

00:01:11.534 --> 00:01:14.267
Even worse,
his friend is still alive.

00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:17.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:19.033
None of it makes sense.

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:20.601
That was Matt Goldich
who wrote that joke.

00:01:20.601 --> 00:01:22.367
That's what he looks like.

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:24.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:30.234
Yeah, I'm going to show
all their pictures

00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:31.968
so that if you see them
in the street,

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:34.567
you're like,
"Let's go to the other..."

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:37.567
Today was the final day of the
Supreme Court's current term.

00:01:37.567 --> 00:01:39.400
I'd say they went out
with a bang,

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.834
but most of them think
that's a sin.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:44.067
[ Audience groans ]

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:46.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.467 --> 00:01:48.801
There's Ian Morgan,
who wrote that.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.434 --> 00:01:58.501
The NYPD Bee Unit
over the weekend

00:01:58.501 --> 00:02:01.734
removed about 2,000 bees
from a Times Square restaurant.

00:02:01.734 --> 00:02:04.501
So now the restaurant
is just called "Apple."

00:02:04.501 --> 00:02:06.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:09.868
That's a good joke.

00:02:09.868 --> 00:02:12.067
I apologize to Ally Hord.

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:16.133
We definitely could have
put that in the monologue.

00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:19.367
Ian, on the other hand...

00:02:19.367 --> 00:02:22.434
NASA, last week, released
the first full-color images

00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:25.100
from its James Webb
Space Telescope.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:28.501
So check it out if you wanna
see where my forehead stops.

00:02:28.501 --> 00:02:30.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:37.234
Mike Scollins wrote that joke.

00:02:37.234 --> 00:02:39.133
Mister...

00:02:39.133 --> 00:02:40.467
Mike wore a tank top to work,

00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:42.400
so that's why we --

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.968
That's why we use that picture.

00:02:44.968 --> 00:02:47.634
Authorities in Florida
arrested a pastor this week

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:50.234
after he allegedly masturbated
at a Starbucks.

00:02:50.234 --> 00:02:54.133
Fortunately, they stopped him
before he could make any sermon.

00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:56.934
[ Audience groans ]

00:02:56.934 --> 00:02:59.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:04.200
Now, there's a litany of reasons
that joke doesn't work.

00:03:05.868 --> 00:03:11.334
One is, no one's ever
used the expression "makes..."

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:14.400
[ Laughing ]

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:15.934
Like, imagine if you said,

00:03:15.934 --> 00:03:17.934
"I walked in on my son,
and he was masturbating."

00:03:17.934 --> 00:03:20.601
"Did you come in before
or after he made some semen?"

00:03:20.601 --> 00:03:22.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.434 --> 00:03:30.367
Who was the culprit
that wrote that joke?

00:03:30.367 --> 00:03:31.634
Yeah.

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:33.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:39.234
When it comes to jokes,
he's got a type.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:44.634
Irish airline Aer Lingus

00:03:44.634 --> 00:03:47.000
this week canceled 18 flights
over two days

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:49.801
due to a spike in
coronavirus cases among staff,

00:03:49.801 --> 00:03:51.868
leading the company
to implement a ban

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:53.934
on lingus between employees.

00:03:53.934 --> 00:03:55.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.267 --> 00:04:00.267
Bryan wrote that joke.

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:01.968
Here's an interesting fact
about Bryan.

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:04.634
His best friend
on the staff is Ian.

00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:06.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.534 --> 00:04:11.567
Probably called each other
on the phone.

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:13.133
"I got a good one
about lingus."

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:15.067
"I got a good one about sermon."

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:23.567
A customer at an Oklahoma
fast-food restaurant this week

00:04:23.567 --> 00:04:25.767
found a bag of crystal meth
with their order.

00:04:25.767 --> 00:04:28.801
"Hey, I only do powders,"
said Mac Tonight.

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:32.067
[ Scattered laughter ]

00:04:32.067 --> 00:04:33.501
You guys remember --
Make some noise

00:04:33.501 --> 00:04:34.934
if you remember Mac Tonight.

00:04:34.934 --> 00:04:36.267
[ Applause ]

00:04:36.267 --> 00:04:39.534
Alright. So the joke
was never gonna work.

00:04:39.534 --> 00:04:42.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.968 --> 00:04:47.767
Also, "Hey, I only do powders"?

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:52.267
That -- Is that -- Has anybody
ever used that for cocaine?

00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:55.934
"You want to go
do some powders?"

00:04:55.934 --> 00:04:58.968
"Right after --
Right after I make some semen."

00:04:58.968 --> 00:05:02.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.901
"There's two things I like --
doing powders and making..."

00:05:05.901 --> 00:05:08.534
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.534 --> 00:05:10.133
It's like
they don't speak English!

00:05:10.133 --> 00:05:14.534
It's like they're writing
using Google Translate.

00:05:14.534 --> 00:05:17.567
It's like they write the jokes,
then translate it to Japanese,

00:05:17.567 --> 00:05:19.601
then translate it
back to English.

00:05:22.868 --> 00:05:26.234
The fast-food restaurant Subway
recently launched a new menu.

00:05:26.234 --> 00:05:28.501
"Well, the kid's menu
is not what you think it is,"

00:05:28.501 --> 00:05:29.868
said Jared.

00:05:29.868 --> 00:05:31.767
[ Audience groans ]

00:05:33.834 --> 00:05:35.267
[ Two hand claps ]

00:05:36.634 --> 00:05:38.767
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.901 --> 00:05:44.767
I don't know what's shocking --
is that a man clapped twice

00:05:44.767 --> 00:05:47.367
or that he waited
for the groan to finish.

00:05:47.367 --> 00:05:49.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:50.868
He's like,
"I don't want my claps

00:05:50.868 --> 00:05:53.968
to get lost in this groan.

00:05:53.968 --> 00:05:56.901
I want everyone to know where
the two claps came from!"

00:05:56.901 --> 00:05:59.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.033 --> 00:06:05.400
Mike Scollins wrote that joke.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:08.133
The Ohio Supreme Court
recently suspended an attorney

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:09.834
for repeatedly driving naked

00:06:09.834 --> 00:06:12.133
and exposing himself
to other drivers.

00:06:12.133 --> 00:06:14.501
Or, as he calls it, "Exhibit D."

00:06:14.501 --> 00:06:16.701
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.901 --> 00:06:24.801
Alright. This has been...
"Surprise Inspection."

00:06:24.801 --> 00:06:26.868
[ Bugle plays ]

00:06:26.868 --> 00:06:28.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

